## Codebase Patterns
- `npm test` bundles and runs `test/index.ts` through `tapout`; Vitest tests
  live beside it and should be run directly with `npx vitest run <file>` for
  targeted checks.
- SPA state follows the template pattern: mutable app behavior is attached to
  the exported `State` function rather than scattered across components.
- The home route owns the Atrament canvas lifecycle and keeps drawing controls
  in component-local signals.
- Netlify Database migrations live under
  `netlify/database/migrations/<prefix>_<slug>/migration.sql`.
- Netlify Blobs helpers should call `getStore(...)` lazily inside exported
  operations, not at module load, so Netlify runtime context is available.
- Netlify Functions can live in nested directories under `netlify/functions`
  to match redirected API paths like `/api/auth/magic-link`.
- Shared backend helpers live under `netlify/lib/*`; keep function handlers
  thin and put reusable storage, email, session, and HTTP helpers there.
- One-time token consumption should be atomic in SQL with a guarded
  `UPDATE ... RETURNING`, checking both `used_at IS NULL` and expiry.
- WebAuthn passkey flows use `@simplewebauthn/server` in Netlify helpers and
  `@simplewebauthn/browser` in routes; challenge state is carried by a short
  lived signed `challenge_token` returned beside the generated options.
- Passkey API handlers are nested under
  `netlify/functions/auth/passkey/<flow>/<step>.ts` to match paths like
  `/api/auth/passkey/register/options`.
- Session-aware API handlers should use `getSession(event)` from
  `netlify/lib/session.ts`; it validates the signed cookie and queries the
  current `users` row so subscription state is not read from stale cookies.
- Frontend auth state is hydrated by `State.fetchAuthStatus(state)`, which
  calls `/api/whoami` and stores the result in `state.currentUser`.
- Frontend paid/free checks should read
  `state.currentUser.value?.subscription_status`; tests that expect paid
  controls to be enabled must populate `state.currentUser`, not only
  `state.auth`.

