- Added a US-001 regression guard that scans package manifests and source for
  removed backend references.
- Files changed: `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `src/state.ts`,
  `src/util.ts`, `src/post-text.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `src/routes/home.ts`,
  `src/routes/index.ts`, `src/routes/login.ts`, `src/routes/login.css`,
  `src/routes/colophon.ts`, deleted old route/function/config files, and
  updated tests.
- Verification: `npx vitest run test/us001-no-atproto.test.ts
  test/home-route.color-picker.test.ts test/login-route.flows.test.ts
  test/state.flows.test.ts test/util.test.ts`; `npm run lint`; `npm test`;
  `npx tsc --noEmit`; browser smoke check at `http://127.0.0.1:8888/`
  confirmed the home route, canvas, and Save button render with no console or
  page errors.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The checked-in `test/test-bundle.js` is generated output if present; the
    tracked browser test entry point is `test/index.ts`.
  - Removing source modules also requires deleting or rewriting old Vitest
    tests because lint scans every `*.ts` file, not just test files that run.
  - Browser-use's Node REPL bridge was not exposed in this session, so the
    browser acceptance check used a Playwright fallback against the same local
    dev server.
  - `tsconfig.json` uses explicit `types` and `typeRoots`; Node-based tests
    need both `@types/node` and the `node` entry in `compilerOptions.types`.
  - `npm test` uses tapout's fixed browser-test port, so run it by itself
    instead of in parallel with other browser-oriented test commands.
